  "verbalization": "Zolmitriptan is classified as a serotonin 1b receptor agonist, and its relationship with Htr1b is mediated through a shared pathway involving serotonin agonists. The evidence suggests that Zolmitriptan, along with Rizatriptan and Eletriptan, belongs to a class of compounds that bind to Htr1b, indicating a potential mechanism of action through the serotonin 1b receptor. The lowest common ancestors of Zolmitriptan and its related compounds point to serotonin agonists, reinforcing the notion that these drugs interact with Htr1b via a common biological target. The consistent binding of these compounds to Htr1b, despite differing receptor subtypes, highlights a broader role of serotonin agonists in modulating Htr1b activity. The integration of these pathways underscores a shared mechanism of action, where the class of serotonin agonists, through their interaction with Htr1b, contributes to the therapeutic effects of Zolmitriptan.",
